    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using mini.diff on its own the plugin isn't enabled after setup() but needs an additional call of `require('mini.diff').enable()`\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI've attached a [minidifftest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26108947/minidifftest.zip) to place in the users home directory, containing \n\n- a `minit.lua` using lazy.nvim do download `mini.diff` only\n- setup mini.diff with basic config\n- simple git repo\n\nWhen calling\n\n```sh\nnvim -u ~/minidifftest/minit.lua ~/minidifftest/testrepo/test.txt \n```\n\nyou'll see no marks from mini.diff\n\n<img width=\"565\" height=\"439\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5729300-01d8-4558-8c7c-4b6daca73b5e\" />\n\nCalling `:lua require(\"mini.diff\").toggle_overlay()` throws an error \n\n```\nE5108: Lua: (mini.diff) Buffer 1 is not enabled.\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'error'\n        ...st/minit/data/nvim-data/lazy/mini.diff/lua/mini/diff.lua:1852: in function 'error'\n        ...st/minit/data/nvim-data/lazy/mini.diff/lua/mini/diff.lua:533: in function 'toggle_overlay'\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n```\n\nbut enables the plugin \n\n<img width=\"564\" height=\"435\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01f7577d-32f5-46c5-8ec1-4f6d713480e0\" />\n\nWhen calling `:lua require(\"mini.diff\").toggle_overlay()` again, the overlay will be enabled\n\n<img width=\"565\" height=\"439\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ee02dd4e-e122-44a9-ab7a-23ac471316bf\" />\n\n",
