            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThe problem is not with 'mini.diff' (and not the fact that it is a standalone repo). Using `keys` in 'lazy.nvim' specification makes plugin [automatically lazy load on when typing those keys](https://lazy.folke.io/spec/lazy_loading). So 'mini.diff' is not enabled on any buffer until `<leader>gd` is pressed or explicitly enabled.\n\nRemoving `keys` field from 'lazy.nvim' spec and making a mapping explicitly solves the issue.",
