        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The repro is a bit confusing, as `minit` itself, when downloaded, is also a git repository.\n\nNew init.lua, using `mini.deps`, adapted from the issue template:\n\n```lua\n\n-- 1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n--     - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n--     - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n--\n-- 2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n--    Populate it with the this file:\n\n-- Clone latest 'mini.deps' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.deps`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/deps/start/mini.deps\"\nlocal clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.deps\", mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.deps` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.deps' is available\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.deps\")\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\n\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\n\nMiniDeps.add(\"nvim-mini/mini.diff\")\n\nrequire(\"mini.diff\").setup({ view = { style = \"sign\" } })\nvim.keymap.set(\n\t\"n\",\n\t\"<leader>ga\",\n\t\"<cmd>lua require('mini.diff').toggle_overlay(0)<cr>\",\n\t{ desc = \"MiniDiff Toggle Overlay\" }\n)\n\n-- 3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n--    Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n```\n\nI added the textfile to `~/minidifftest/testrepro/text.txt`\n\nRun: `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro ~/minidifftest/testrepro/test.txt`\n\nType `:lua require(\"mini.diff\").toggle_overlay()` \n\nResults: The \"not enabled\" error you mentioned.\n\nHowever, when I add the textfile to a git repository(`git init .` inside `~/minidifftest/`, that error no longer appears.\n\nFrom `:h MiniDiff.config`:\n\n```lua\n\n  -- Source(s) for how reference text is computed/updated/etc\n  -- Uses content from Git index by default\n  source = nil,\n```\n\nThe error occurs when there is no git repository yet.\n\nI don't think it matters whether mini.diff is standalone or used as part of mini.nvim....",
